   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the real property tax law, in relation to permitting special\ndistricts to adopt a local law providing for an exemption for improvements to\nresidential real property for the purpose of facilitating accessibility of\nsuch property to a physically disabled owner",
    "basePrintNo": "S6452",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6452-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §459, RPT L",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Tax Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6452\n\nSPONSOR: KAPLAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the real property tax law, in relation to permitting\nspecial districts to adopt a local law providing for an exemption for\nimprovements to residential real property for the purpose of facilitat-\ning accessibility of such property to a physically disabled owner\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this legislation to permit special districts to adopt\nlocal laws providing for an exemption for improvements to residential\nreal property for facilitating accessibility of such property to a phys-\nically disabled owner.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Subdivisions 1 and 3 of section 459 of the Real Property Tax\nLaw is amended by adding special districts to the current language that\nincludes counties, cities, towns and villages.\n\nSection 2. Establishes the effective date.\n\n \nDIFFERENCE BETWEEN ORIGINAL AND AMENDED VERSION (IF APPLICABLE):\n\nThe change is technical and does not change the purpose of the bill in\nany way. 'Special District' was placed later in the sentence.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrently, after a public hearing, a county, city, town or village may\nadopt a local law, or a school district may adopt a resolution, provid-\ning a residential exemption from taxation to the extent of any increase\nin value caused by the accommodation and accessibility of a physically\ndisabled person.\n\nOften, persons with disabilities must make costly modifications and\nrenovations to their homes. A few examples of these modifications could\ninclude the installation of ramps, grab bars, or alterations to their\nlighting and heating systems\n\nThis legislation will simply add 'special districts' to the current\nlanguage.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nA.10335 and S. 8219 of 2017/2018\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nThe fiscal implications associated with the passage of this legislation\nare expected to be minimal.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
